- BUG:
    -if expecting expression but got eof will make the compiler get stuck
        even doing checks for eof seems to not work unless the file ended with a line feed
    - a statement such as 'var my_slice: []i32 = [1, 2, 3]' will actually compile to an array instead of a slice.
        - this should just throw a compile error as assigning array to struct. only other way around should be allowed.

- current roadmap:
    - generics
    - traits
    - enum payloads
    - sum types
    - match expr and other pattern matching
    - StringId
    - refactor compiler directives and implement reflection
    - user defined attributes

- tech debt:
    - replace as many instances of dynamic_cast with alternatives. 1) use enums for all nodes such as STMT::VarDecl. 2) use virtual methods where possible.
    - change many expression types into unary and postfix expressions instead of doing them within parse_primary.
    - theres a lot of allocations made when using stl containers. replace them with custom allocators and reuse memory more often.
    - the compeval is currently very incomplete.
    - theres too much repeated work between the ast and analyzer.
    - the compiler wastes too much memory:
        - once a module is compiled a lot of local nodes can be erased and reused by the node arena.
            only nodes that can be seen from other modules must be kept.
        - some types should be cached.
    - pointer arithmetic type mismatch. coercion sucks right now.
    - function parameter mutability testing is very wonky right now. can pass a imut T to a function expecting T.
    - the analysis for member access has become extremely messy. same with symbol analysis.

- design issues:
    - literals and type coercion need addressing.
        use a better way to coerce types such as in the analyzer check if the checked type and the context type dont match
        then try to do a coercion.
        literals should be coerced to whatever type is is most viable in its context.
        integer suffixes should also be added for greater ease of use.
    - function parameters should be immutable by default. perhaps use shadowing or a special keyword to make them mutable.
    - imports currently work from the directory the compiler was invoked from rather than relative to the current module. pls fix.

- warnings to add:

