- misc:
    - currently type coercion is unreliable. perhaps implement type coercion inside the analyzer so when a node is visited
        it will check the context type and if it is not equal to its own type it will do a coercion.
    - undefined keyword that can be used when setting the initial value of a variable. this will make it not initialize to its default value.
        useful for very large values that do not need default initialization.
    - allow a method to be taken as a function pointer if the type of the desired function pointer has the methods type as the first parameter
        example:
            var fn_ptr: fn(user: User, value: i32)

            fn_ptr = User::set_value

            fn_ptr(my_user, 100)

        in this case the method degrades to a normal function so it can be taken as a function pointer

    - make pointers have index operators.
    - unicode.
    - implement a custom version of vector called FrameVec that relies on temporary short lived allocations that allocate from a large arena.
        this is very useful for temporary buffers in recursive function calls that cannot be static.
        so the memory allocated will be cheap and predictable.
        alternatively i can just make a custom frame allocator for std::vector but i have to see which is more ideal.
    - implement destructuring of all aggregate types.
    - add a way for modules to declare information about themselves:
        - one useful thing can be a module specifying that it needs a certain link flag if it is ever imported.
        - useful for cmath so it can only link against it if it is used.
    - implement arithmetic operations for nested arrays such as [4][4]f32.
    - currently a lot of types have wonky sizes. implement more accurate sizes.
    - pure functions with the pure attribute. perhaps even automatic pure detection.
    - change keyword attributes to not actually be real keywords so they can be used for symbols. possibly just use structs defined inside core package.
    - bitwise operators
    - improve literal analysis. literals should be coerced into anytype if they fit.
    - correctly handle float min and max value properties. currently its the same as integers which is obviously wrong.
    - replace recursive descent with operator precedent parsing (pratt parsing)
    - break and continue to label. possibly goto? probably a bad idea anyway
    - automatic va_list creation when passing ... to another function
    - manual va_list support
    - compile time for loops
    - floor div with //
    - stringify operator
    - currently shadowing works fine. but this was unintended. in the future i might want to consider disallowing it.
    - integral literal suffixes
    - typeof operator
    - assert statement
    - integral literals in other bases such as hex or binary
    - improve api for compiler functions
    - real type that can accept any integral value and automatically does the correct code gen depending on its current value
    - vardiac arguments
    - runtime type information through a Type type
    - typeid system
    - type is expression
    - for loop where clause
    - references
    - auto references
    - cuda support
    - openmp support
    - take for loop element as a pointer or reference
    - alow cast to only cast to a qualifier. such as cast(imut).
    - implement a safety analyzer that has to be switched that will throw warnings on possible safety issues found:
        - this analyzer could hopefully do rust level safety checks but as an optional stage before shipping a new version of software,
        - analysis to see if a pointer to stack memory is escaping its scope.
        - nil analysis to see if a pointer could possibly be nil at a certain point.
        - lifetime analysis to see if a reference or pointer will out live its actual memory.

